; ted-screenopen2-label-blitz2 (#1007, the fix under blitz2): the label
; column makes TED reopen its screen right after blitz2 hands it the
; start file (showmice in .tomain).  blitz2 under inject (alerts
; answered), a source with a label; the chip allocations of 20000..45000
; bytes after the first (the start's bit map) fail, so the reopen fails.
; Correct: the alert "Not enough memory for operation!", TED ends with
; return code -1 and blitz2 ends normally; the original goes on without
; a screen.
; @fixed #1007
; @file bo.bas ".a\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=20000-45000/chip+1 blitz2:blitz2 @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 5 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=0"
timeout 20
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait exit
